@猫馬鹿おじさんJapan’s system of military sexual slavery (“comfort women”) was systematically organized by the state, and records documenting the forced mobilization of women remain in official U.S. government documents. It was a crime against humanity, and there are countless historical records and testimonies not only from Korea, but also from China and Russia.

Some traumatic experiences remain painfully vivid no matter how much time passes—that is a well-known phenomenon in neuroscience.

Seeing you deny and mock such well-documented history, I have to wonder: were your parents exposed to the Hiroshima atomic bomb before you were born? 😂 Hiroshima atomic bomb again, boom boom.❤❤
